course: dictionary
lesson: 5915
title: Marmalade in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Marmalade is a kind of jam made from oranges or other citrus fruits, like lemons or limes, with thin strips of peel in it. The context helps here: «Alice took a jar labelled "ORANGE MARMALADE" from a shelf» tells you it is food kept in a jar, and the word orange is a clue to the fruit.
explain: Use the swap check. «Alice took a jar of orange jam from a shelf» still makes sense, so jam is a good meaning. Marmalade is a special kind of jam, though, because it has peel in it.
explain: Marmalade can also be a colour, an orange colour often used for ginger cats. So «a marmalade cat» is an orange or ginger cat, not a cat made of jam. Always check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Marmalade is a jam made from citrus fruit with thin strips of peel in it.
fact: «Orange marmalade» is one common kind, and «marmalade on toast» is a traditional breakfast in Britain, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: Seville oranges are bitter, and they are used to make marmalade in January.
fact: Paddington Bear loves marmalade sandwiches.
fact: «A marmalade cat» is an orange or ginger cat, because marmalade can also mean an orange colour.
exercise: «Alice took a jar labelled "ORANGE MARMALADE" from a shelf.» What is marmalade? | A kind of bread baked in an oven | A kind of cheese made from milk | A kind of soup | *A kind of jam made from citrus fruits, with peel in it
exercise: In «a marmalade cat», what does marmalade describe? | *An orange colour, like a ginger cat | A cat that is very fast | A cat that makes jam
exercise: Which breakfast is «marmalade on toast»? | Cold soup | *Jam made from citrus fruit spread on toast | A fried egg | Boiled rice
test: What kind of food is marmalade? | Soup | Meat | Cake | *Jam
test: What does «a marmalade cat» mean? | A cat that eats jam | A very fast cat | *An orange or ginger cat | A cat with a long tail
exam: Which clue best helps you work out that marmalade is a food? | Alice was very tired | Alice falls down a rabbit hole | *A jar labelled "ORANGE MARMALADE" that Alice takes from a shelf | The children stood still
